    <div id=3D"designing" class=3D"cmp-text ">
        <h2>Designing the tech stack for what=E2=80=99s possible</h2>
<p>For enterprises, designing an adaptable tech stack is less about predict=
ion and more about architecture and engineering principles.</p>
<p>One way to understand the shift is through how the internet itself is ev=
olving. A recent IEEE Spectrum<sup><a href=3D"https://www.deloitte.com/us/e=
n/insights/topics/technology-management/digital-infrastructure-strategy.htm=
l#endnote-19" aria-label=3D"Endnotes reference number 19">19</a></sup> arti=
cle outlines a progression from early connectivity to today=E2=80=99s infle=
ction point, and where we could be headed (figure 1).</p>

